# Real-Time Deepfake Detection Platform

**SIH 2026 | Problem Statement USICT028 | Category: AI Safety & Media Verification**

A real-time deepfake detection platform for live video streams. Analyzes each frame using a Vision Transformer, aggregates predictions temporally, and triggers alerts on sustained high-confidence detections.

## Features

- 📹 Live webcam capture with face detection
- 📁 Upload video file mode (with real-time or full-analysis playback)
- 🤖 Pre-trained Vision Transformer model (`prithivMLmods/Deep-Fake-Detector-Model`)
- 🎨 Color-coded bounding boxes (green = REAL, orange = SUSPICIOUS, red = FAKE)
- 📊 Live metrics: confidence, smoothed score, FPS, model latency, face count
- 🚨 Temporal alert logic (N consecutive high-confidence frames → alert)
- 📝 Timestamped alert log

## Setup

### 1. Prerequisites
- Python 3.13
- Windows / Mac / Linux
- Optional: NVIDIA GPU for faster inference

### 2. Install

```bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate       # Windows PowerShell
# source venv/bin/activate  # Mac/Linux

pip install -r requirements.txt
```

*(If PowerShell blocks the activate script, run `Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned` first.)*

### 3. Run

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

App opens at `http://localhost:8501`. First run downloads the model (~350 MB).

## Config (edit in `app.py`)

| Setting | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `WINDOW_SIZE` | 5 | Rolling window for score smoothing |
| `ALERT_THRESHOLD` | 0.6 | Smoothed score above this = alert territory |
| `CONSECUTIVE_ALERTS_NEEDED` | 3 | Consecutive over-threshold checks before firing an alert |
| `FRAME_SKIP` | 10 | Run model every Nth frame (set to 1 on GPU) |

## GPU Migration

When moving to a CUDA-capable GPU:

```bash
pip uninstall torch torchvision -y
pip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121
```

Then in `app.py`, set `FRAME_SKIP = 1` and increase webcam resolution to 1280x720.

Model auto-detects the GPU — no other code changes needed.

## Architecture
Live Video / Uploaded File
↓
Frame Extraction (OpenCV)
↓
Face Detection (Haar Cascade)
↓
Pre-processing (crop, resize to 224x224)
↓
Deepfake Detection (Vision Transformer)
↓
Temporal Aggregation (rolling window)
↓
Alert Logic (streak-based)
↓
Dashboard (Streamlit)


## Known Limitations

- CPU inference is slow (~500-800 ms/frame). Real-time performance requires GPU.
- Haar Cascade face detector struggles with side profiles and heavy occlusion. Production should use MediaPipe or MTCNN.
- Model is pre-trained on general deepfake datasets — fine-tuning on domain-specific data would improve accuracy.

